insert into public.tips (id, unit_id, title_en, body_md, status) values
  ('e269a333-71df-57b4-a283-d27e6172279f', '68cbb710-d119-5f34-a613-de8835c78c69', 'Querían que estudiara', 'Growing up, every wish was in the past: **mis viejos querían que estudiara** — *my parents wanted me to study*; **no querían que saliera de noche** — *they didn''t want me going out at night*. The second verb follows the first into the past.', 'draft'),
  ('1ee17a4e-61a4-582d-82c1-7cd20734095b', '68cbb710-d119-5f34-a613-de8835c78c69', 'One trick, every verb', 'Take the *ellos* preterite and swap **-ron** for **-ra**: *salieron* → **saliera**, *volvieron* → **volviera**, *dijeron* → **dijera**. With vos add an **-s**: **estudiaras, dijeras, fueras**. For *ellos*: **querían que vinieran todos**.', 'draft'),
  ('f4e91a43-2aa1-517a-8400-3d242229a9a1', '68cbb710-d119-5f34-a613-de8835c78c69', 'Pedir permiso', 'A porteño family can be **estricta**: *para salir tenía que pedir **permiso***, and my mum **quería que volviera temprano** — which never happened.', 'draft'),
  ('2df58fe2-bf8f-5caa-8c0e-83306081923b', '345642d1-7c5d-58fc-936d-78082196d9c0', 'Por más que', '**Por más que** — *no matter how much* — is *aunque* turned up: **por más que me cueste, sigo** — *however hard it is, I keep going*. A maybe takes the subjunctive, a fact doesn''t: *por más que **entreno**, engordo* — I do train; it just doesn''t show.', 'draft'),
  ('162494b0-6ab0-5984-a9da-823d59556384', '345642d1-7c5d-58fc-936d-78082196d9c0', 'Aunque sea', '**Aunque sea** — *at least, even if it''s only* — is the deal you make with yourself: *hoy no tengo ganas, pero **aunque sea** un rato voy*. And the other half of it: **aunque no me dé el tiempo** — *even if I don''t have the time*.', 'draft'),
  ('a86f3f75-92ae-5f8d-ad92-17fed3596c6b', '345642d1-7c5d-58fc-936d-78082196d9c0', 'Sin embargo, así y todo', 'Both start the second half: **sin embargo** — *however* — and the more spoken **así y todo** — *even so*: *hice dieta; **así y todo**, engordé*.', 'draft'),
  ('e45f0679-9535-5a33-aedf-9eb551a41541', '558006ff-a18d-5fc9-ae98-edf66c5a28dc', '¿Hace cuánto?', 'Every porteño asks it: **¿hace cuánto que estudiás?** — *how long have you been studying?* Answer either way: **hace un año que estudio** or **llevo un año estudiando**. Or count from a moment: **desde que llegué** — *since I arrived*.', 'draft'),
  ('e4aaa23a-d398-5826-a0e6-71432f62e794', '558006ff-a18d-5fc9-ae98-edf66c5a28dc', 'Sigo, seguimos, siguen', 'Everyone can keep at it: **sigo practicando**, **seguimos buscando** laburo, *mis amigos* **siguen tratando de** entenderme. And stop: **dejaron de** venir — *they stopped coming*.', 'draft'),
  ('af169ce1-a481-5903-bf9a-f531f72990af', '558006ff-a18d-5fc9-ae98-edf66c5a28dc', 'Volví a', '**Volver a** + an infinitive is *to do it again*: **volví a estudiar** — *I went back to studying*; **vuelvo a empezar** — *I''m starting over*.', 'draft'),
  ('df9106c3-5bfc-57cc-b3da-428704d81c8e', 'ea7df981-3c2b-53d4-96e1-cee2e5d5bd8e', 'Querían que, por más que', '**Mis viejos querían que estudiara** — the wish is in the past, so the second verb is too. **Por más que me cueste** — however hard it is: a maybe takes the subjunctive.', 'draft'),
  ('85402fa0-6355-51d2-b439-9abb4c3aa126', 'ea7df981-3c2b-53d4-96e1-cee2e5d5bd8e', '¿Hace cuánto?', '**Hace un año que estudio** says the same as **llevo un año estudiando**. **Seguimos buscando**, **volví a empezar**.', 'draft'),
  ('05178197-f8a8-5b0e-84c9-cf4f1f9d70ad', '796fb7f5-7211-54d8-83dc-d15338978f46', 'Coman, prueben, agarren', 'At the table the host never stops: **coman**, **prueben**, **tomen algo**, **agarren pan**. Same rule as *pasen*: -ar verbs end in **-en**, the rest in **-an** — **coman**, **hagan** lugar, **vayan** sentándose.', 'draft'),
  ('9cca76e8-1bf3-5576-9d7c-c338276503e1', '796fb7f5-7211-54d8-83dc-d15338978f46', 'No se olviden', 'With a *no* in front the verb stays the same and the pronoun jumps ahead: **apúrense**, but **no se olviden** — *don''t forget*; **no dejen nada** — *don''t leave anything*.', 'draft'),
  ('1a5ebe3a-b4e7-546a-b4ed-cb9dba0344f7', '796fb7f5-7211-54d8-83dc-d15338978f46', 'Buen provecho', 'Before the first bite: **¡buen provecho!** — *enjoy!* And when the host says **sírvanse** — *help yourselves* — nobody waits to be asked twice.', 'draft'),
  ('94763621-e0b3-590a-947d-816f3e66782c', 'e3ba7db9-0794-5f78-95a6-dbd6a3e616be', 'Te hacés el, me hice el', '**Hacerse el** works for everyone: **te hacés el sordo** — *you act like you can''t hear*; **me hice el distraído** — *I pretended not to notice*. The one who acts like he''s seen it all **se hace el canchero**. To stop it: **no te hagas el gil** — *don''t play dumb*.', 'draft'),
  ('86ee83db-35b7-58e6-8985-2d6d6006e0ac', 'e3ba7db9-0794-5f78-95a6-dbd6a3e616be', 'Como si no…', '**Como si** with a *no*: **como si no pasara nada**, **como si no me viera**, **como si no le importara**. And the comeback: **¡ni que fueras mi viejo!** — *it''s not like you''re my dad!*', 'draft'),
  ('8e0594ac-1009-51d2-b934-d91eaaa7f29c', 'e3ba7db9-0794-5f78-95a6-dbd6a3e616be', '¡Qué caradura!', 'Someone who does it with a straight face is a **caradura** — *shameless, cheeky*: **¡qué caradura!** Between friends it''s almost a compliment.', 'draft'),
  ('d4f3c5be-cc6e-55ca-b459-5f8dcfb65deb', '68c86280-614b-5223-b263-aed0f05b7b3c', 'El de, la de', 'Drop the noun, keep the article: **el de la vidriera** — *the one in the window*; **la de la izquierda** — *the one on the left*; **las de** allá. It matches what it stands for, like *el que*: **la que te probaste**.', 'draft'),
  ('94008fd4-0872-5a8a-9ec2-29c8968f8904', '68c86280-614b-5223-b263-aed0f05b7b3c', 'Elijan, como quieras', 'To a friend: **elegí el que quieras**. To two friends: **elijan los que quieran**. Not chosen yet, so the subjunctive: **el que elijas**, **la que prefieras**. And when you really don''t mind: **como quieras** — *whatever you like*.', 'draft'),
  ('d5688bae-b7ba-57fc-b691-b14418254954', '79cfb639-7996-5ed9-85ae-f73c0cf69e58', 'Coman, no se olviden', 'For a group: **coman**, **prueben**, **sírvanse**, **no se olviden**. The *no* doesn''t change the verb, only where the pronoun goes.', 'draft'),
  ('3f1a2506-1043-5f7c-8f88-5002421068f6', '79cfb639-7996-5ed9-85ae-f73c0cf69e58', 'Como si no, el de', '**Como si no me viera** — *as if he didn''t see me*. **El de la vidriera** — *the one in the window*; **el que quieras** — *whichever you want*.', 'draft'),
  ('4dc827e6-3705-5cb5-a90d-65b3e54eb13b', 'd2d1e75f-f8c3-5507-9e3a-6019ac0c40a0', 'Hubiéramos, hubieran', 'For *we*: **si hubiéramos salido antes, no hubiéramos perdido el vuelo**. For *they*: **si hubieran avisado, hubiéramos venido**. Still **hubiera** in both halves, the porteño way.', 'draft'),
  ('70cedfaf-7bda-5824-a31d-da0c4fef72bd', 'd2d1e75f-f8c3-5507-9e3a-6019ac0c40a0', 'More participles', '-ar verbs take **-ado**, the rest **-ido**: **tomado, reservado, quedado, perdido, conseguido**. *Traer* keeps its accent: **traído**. *Si hubiera tomado un taxi…*, *si me hubiera quedado en casa…*', 'draft'),
  ('d338d3db-f4ad-55cc-8eab-5ce4e8d0c03c', 'd2d1e75f-f8c3-5507-9e3a-6019ac0c40a0', 'Qué mala suerte', 'When nobody''s to blame: **¡qué mala suerte!** And at Ezeiza the board says what every porteño expects: the flight is **demorado** — *delayed*.', 'draft'),
  ('5ca0fdb9-29ca-51ab-ad72-6fc098d18dd4', 'eedc812b-9def-5602-bd94-b8fc7ba8e7b6', 'Además, sobre todo', 'To stack up reasons: **además** — *besides* — adds one more; **sobre todo** — *above all* — picks the one that counts: *me gusta, **sobre todo** por la gente*. Porteños also say **más que nada** — *mainly*.', 'draft'),
  ('65ee37e5-32e4-5795-acaa-8f3a37e6f50c', 'eedc812b-9def-5602-bd94-b8fc7ba8e7b6', 'Por lo menos, la verdad', '**Por lo menos** — *at least* — finds the good side: *pagan poco, pero **por lo menos** queda cerca*. **La verdad** — *honestly* — says what you really think: ***la verdad**, no me conviene*.', 'draft'),
  ('6b3cc89e-06da-5b09-90a5-fb94272d6eb3', 'de1cac02-1435-56ef-9682-17ea2bc59bc4', 'Una consulta', 'At any **ventanilla**, open with **una consulta** — *a quick question* — and ask for the **requisitos**, *what they need*. They''ll say **el original y una copia**, and they mean both.', 'draft'),
  ('0a7f761b-d9c7-516c-b579-5874def00152', 'de1cac02-1435-56ef-9682-17ea2bc59bc4', '¿Cuánto demora?', 'Porteños say **demorar** for how long something takes: **¿cuánto demora la residencia?** The honest answer is *depende*. You **presentás** the papers, and when they finally **atienden** you, it''s over in five minutes.', 'draft'),
  ('05a15524-d45f-5861-a2f4-81ee55090fe9', '4a9c7846-0bb3-5a60-94df-2f6897d2a8dc', 'Hubiéramos, hubieran', '**Si hubiéramos salido antes, no hubiéramos perdido el vuelo** — *we* and *they* take **hubiéramos, hubieran**, in both halves.', 'draft'),
  ('ded88745-e472-512f-a433-ecb38187881c', '4a9c7846-0bb3-5a60-94df-2f6897d2a8dc', 'Además, por lo menos', '**Además** adds a reason; **por lo menos** finds the good side; **la verdad** says what you really think.', 'draft'),
  ('b93ba3b3-6a29-5ed3-a84e-307bfd07bb7b', '4356c8d2-a33c-5a38-8b20-f4ac90387e6f', 'Me equivoqué', 'The hardest words in any argument: **me equivoqué** — *I was wrong*. To a friend: **te equivocás** — *you''re wrong*. Giving ground: **reconozco que** tenés razón, or just **te doy la razón**.', 'draft'),
  ('1257cd1c-a853-5a83-8483-1b544c971a7b', '4356c8d2-a33c-5a38-8b20-f4ac90387e6f', '¡Nada que ver!', '**¡Nada que ver!** — *that''s got nothing to do with it!* — is how porteños throw out a point. **En eso** tenés razón concedes just the one. **No seas cabeza dura** — *don''t be so stubborn*.', 'draft'),
  ('3a35b239-66d5-5069-9a26-1a37d49b5555', '4356c8d2-a33c-5a38-8b20-f4ac90387e6f', 'A ver, pensándolo bien', '**A ver** — *let''s see* — slows an argument down; **pensándolo bien** — *thinking about it* — is how you change sides without losing face. **Sos un exagerado** speeds it back up.', 'draft')
